# Helm dependency output — `helm dependency update` vendors the library chart
# and writes a lock. Both are reproducible from Chart.yaml, and committing the
# vendored copy means the library exists twice with nothing keeping them equal.
#
# Led by `**/` rather than by `repo-gitops/`: these two lines were anchored to
# the old `charts/` at the repo root, and the day the tree moved they matched
# nothing — seven vendored platform-service tarballs sat one `git add -A` away
# from the history with git reporting them as ordinary untracked files. `**/`
# also matches zero directories, so the same two lines keep working unchanged
# from the root of repo-gitops once it is a git repo of its own.
**/charts/*/charts/
**/charts/*/Chart.lock

# Assistant configuration — local working setup, not part of the deliverable.
# These describe how this repository is worked on rather than what it does, and
# they belong to the machine, not the project.
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
WORKING-RULES.md
.claude/
.codex/
.cursor/
.cursorrules
.aider*
.github/copilot-instructions.md

# Credentials — never commit
# `kubeconfig*` and `.env*` are single patterns on purpose: the earlier
# `kubeconfig` + `kubeconfig-*` pair missed `kubeconfig.yaml`, and `.env` +
# `.env.*` missed `.envrc`. A credentials pattern that covers every name but
# one is the same as not having it.
# None of the four carries a slash, so all four match at any depth — the repo
# split moved every other pattern in this file and left these four correct.
*.pem
*.key
kubeconfig*
.env*

# Node / Next.js build output — reinstalled by `npm ci` and rebuilt by
# `next build`, so nothing here is worth a commit. Unignored, `node_modules/`
# collapses to a single `??` line in `git status`, which is how tens of
# thousands of files get in behind one `git add -A` without looking like much.
# Not anchored to repo-webui/web-ui: a second frontend would hit this the same
# way.
node_modules/
.next/
.turbo/
npm-debug.log*
# `output: "export"` writes the static site to `out/` instead of `.next/`.
# Anchored under the frontend repo so a real directory named `out` elsewhere in
# the tree does not silently disappear from git.
/repo-webui/*/out/

# Go binaries built on the host — `go build ./cmd/payment` without `-o` drops a
# ~40 MB executable beside go.mod, named after the package. Every path is
# spelled out because a bare `payment` would also match
# `repo-api/services/cmd/payment/`, hiding the source the binary was built from.
# A new service under cmd/ needs its name added here.
/repo-api/services/auth
/repo-api/services/catalog
/repo-api/services/order
/repo-api/services/payment
/repo-api/notification/notification
# `go test -c` leaves a `<pkg>.test` binary; `-coverprofile` leaves the profile.
*.test
coverage.out

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/
.zcode/

# GUI-test evidence (browser screenshots) — session artifacts, not source.
gui-test-screenshots/
